      <reaction compartment="compartment_7660" fast="false" id="reaction_349455" metaid="metaid_40" name="Phosphorylation of MDM4 by ATM" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Human MDM4 (MDMX) is phosphorylated on serine residue S403 by ATM. This site is important for MDM2-mediated ubiquitination of MDM4 after induction of double strand DNA breaks (Pereg et al. 2005, Chen et al. 2005).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
